{"abstract":"Providing rich, constructive feedback to students is essential for supporting and enhancing their learning. Recent advancements in Generative Artificial Intelligence (AI), particularly with large language models (LLMs), present new opportunities to deliver scalable, repeatable, and instant feedback, effectively making abundant a resource that has historically been scarce and costly. From a technical perspective, this approach is now feasible due to breakthroughs in AI and Natural Language Processing (NLP). While the potential educational benefits are compelling, implementing these technologies also introduces a host of ethical considerations that must be thoughtfully addressed. One of the core advantages of AI systems is their ability to automate routine and mundane tasks, potentially freeing up human educators for more nuanced work. However, the ease of automation risks a 'tyranny of the majority', where the diverse needs of minority or unique learners are overlooked, as they may be harder to systematize and less straightforward to accommodate. Ensuring inclusivity and equity in AI-generated feedback, therefore, becomes a critical aspect of responsible AI implementation in education. The process of developing machine learning models that produce valuable, personalized, and authentic feedback also requires significant input from human domain experts. Decisions around whose expertise is incorporated, how it is captured, and when it is applied have profound implications for the relevance and quality of the resulting feedback. Additionally, the maintenance and continuous refinement of these models are necessary to adapt feedback to evolving contextual, theoretical, and student-related factors. Without ongoing adaptation, feedback risks becoming obsolete or mismatched with the current needs of diverse student populations. Addressing these challenges is essential not only for ethical integrity but also for building the operational trust needed to integrate AI-driven systems as valuable tools in contemporary education. Thoughtful planning and deliberate choices are needed to ensure that these solutions truly benefit all students, allowing AI to support an inclusive and dynamic learning environment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lindsay, Euan","Zhang, Mike","Johri, Aditya","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-686961"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","George Mason University"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence AI","Artificial intelligence","Educational technology","Ethics","Generative AI","Human Computer Interaction","Natural Language Processing","Student Feedback"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the responsible development of automated student feedback with generative ai","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.15334","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["EDL, MZ, and JB are supported by the research grant (VIL57392) from VILLUM FONDEN. AJ is partly supported by US NSF Awards 2319137, 1954556, and USDA/NIFA Award 2021-67021-35329. Any opinions, findings, and conclusions or recommendations expressed in this material are those of the authors and do not necessarily reflect the views of the funding agencies."],"id":"S01-000.00-686961","identifier":[{"id":"105008229311","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a705f284-2cfe-443c-82cd-1063f015b39e"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Artificial Intelligence (AI)","Educational Technology","Ethics","Generative AI","Human-Computer Interaction","Natural Language Processing","Student Feedback"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1A81B067CA256735C3D76CEFCA6D2F63"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2308.15334","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, Institute for Advanced Study in PBL","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Aalborg Centre for Problem Based Learning in Engineering Science and Sustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"george mason university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"George Mason University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Euan","key":"lindsaypau","last":"Lindsay","locid":"3cd826f8-e16d-46cc-8b71-956ecaded5e5","name":"Lindsay, Euan","orcid":"0000-0003-3266-164X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aditya","key":"johripau","last":"Johri","name":"Johri, Aditya","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/educon62633.2025.11016572","eisbn":["9798331539498"],"publisher":"IEEE Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Special Session: Generative AI and Ethical Integration in Higher Education: Navigating Innovation and Responsibility","title":"Proceedings of the IEEE Global Engineering Education Conference (EDUCON 2025)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008229311"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a705f284-2cfe-443c-82cd-1063f015b39e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Responsible Development of Automated Student Feedback with Generative AI","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-686961","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) requires that public companies file financial reports tagging numbers with the machine readable inline eXtensible Business Reporting Language (iXBRL) standard. However, the highly complex and highly granular taxonomy defined by iXBRL limits label transferability across domains. In this paper, we introduce the Hierarchical Financial Key Performance Indicator (HiFi-KPI) dataset, designed to facilitate numerical KPI extraction at specified levels of granularity from unstructured financial text. Our approach organizes a 218,126-label hierarchy using a taxonomy based grouping method, investigating which taxonomy layer provides the most meaningful structure. HiFi-KPI comprises ~1.8M paragraphs and ~5M entities, each linked to a label in the iXBRL-specific calculation and presentation taxonomies. We provide baselines using encoder-based approaches and structured extraction using Large Language Models (LLMs). To simplify LLM inference and evaluation, we additionally release HiFi-KPI Lite, a manually curated subset with four expert-mapped labels. We publicly release all artifacts.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aavang, Rasmus T.","Rizzi, Giovanni","Bøggild, Rasmus","Iolov, Alexandre","Zhang, Mike","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794818"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["NLP","Quantitative finance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hifi kpi a dataset for hierarchical kpi extraction from earnings filings","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-794818","ids":["aau-8ed59039-bc18-4e30-976c-f595d46574ca"],"keyword":["NLP","Quantitative Finance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-57DC572E956E7D8738F343B50FF3741C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["ALIPES ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus T.","key":"aavangpau","last":"Aavang","locid":"781a5033-4427-4d9b-9cb4-70f67089ace5","name":"Aavang, Rasmus T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"rizzipau","last":"Rizzi","name":"Rizzi, Giovanni","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bøggildpau","last":"Bøggild","name":"Bøggild, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandre","key":"iolovpau","last":"Iolov","name":"Iolov, Alexandre","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2502.15411","status":"s"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","alipes aps"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-8ed59039-bc18-4e30-976c-f595d46574ca"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"HiFi-KPI: A Dataset for Hierarchical KPI Extraction from Earnings Filings","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794818","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Recent studies on large language model (LLM) reasoning capabilities have demonstrated promising improvements in model performance by leveraging a lengthy thinking process and additional computational resources during inference, primarily in tasks involving mathematical reasoning (Muennighoff et al., 2025). However, it remains uncertain if longer reasoning chains inherently enhance factual accuracy, particularly beyond mathematical contexts. In this work, we thoroughly examine LLM reasoning within complex open-domain question-answering (QA) scenarios. We initially distill reasoning traces from advanced, large-scale reasoning models (QwQ-32B and DeepSeek-R1-671B), then fine-tune a variety of models ranging from smaller, instruction-tuned variants to larger architectures based on Qwen2.5. To enrich reasoning traces, we introduce factual information from knowledge graphs in the form of paths into our reasoning traces. Our experimental setup includes four baseline approaches and six different instruction-tuned models evaluated across a benchmark of six datasets, encompassing over 22.6K questions. Overall, we carry out 168 experimental runs and analyze approximately 1.7 million reasoning traces. Our findings indicate that, within a single run, smaller reasoning models achieve noticeable improvements in factual accuracy compared to their original instruction-tuned counterparts. Moreover, our analysis demonstrates that adding test-time compute and token budgets factual accuracy consistently improves by 2-8%, further confirming the effectiveness of test-time scaling for enhancing performance and consequently improving reasoning accuracy in open-domain QA tasks. We release all the experimental artifacts for further research.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Bjerva, Johannes","Biswas, Russa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805217"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scaling reasoning can improve factuality in large language models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-805217","ids":["aau-88a5d75e-64f3-4b0d-a5b1-21ef2052fb28"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-502F8D33F2D8F9B5DD664F1D16DC6AEC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Russa","key":"biswaspau","last":"Biswas","locid":"7ba011ce-d8c8-4e94-9167-6f9a7595e076","name":"Biswas, Russa","orcid":"0000-0002-7421-3389","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2505.11140","status":"s"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-88a5d75e-64f3-4b0d-a5b1-21ef2052fb28"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Scaling Reasoning can Improve Factuality in Large Language Models","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805217","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We present SnakModel, a Danish large language model (LLM) based on Llama2-7B, which we continuously pre-train on 13.6B Danish words, and further tune on 3.7M Danish instructions. As best practices for creating LLMs for smaller language communities have yet to be established, we examine the effects of early modeling and training decisions on downstream performance throughout the entire training pipeline, including (1) the creation of a strictly curated corpus of Danish text from diverse sources; (2) the language modeling and instruction-tuning training process itself, including the analysis of intermediate training dynamics, and ablations across different hyperparameters; (3) an evaluation on eight language and culturally-specific tasks. Across these experiments SnakModel achieves the highest overall performance, outperforming multiple contemporary Llama2-7B-based models. By making SnakModel, the majority of our pre-training corpus, and the associated code available under open licenses, we hope to foster further research and development in Danish Natural Language Processing, and establish training guidelines for languages with similar resource constraints.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Müller-Eberstein, Max","Bassignana, Elisa","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S02-087.89-813507"],"event":{"acronym":"NODALIDA","title":"Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Large Language Model"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"snakmodel lessons learned from training an open danish large language model","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.80/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.89-813507","ids":["aau-f723cc80-f5e3-4c09-996e-b1ba16b9c7f2","itu-bb98c006-6693-41e0-b20c-84f6825ba953"],"keyword":["Danish language model","large language model","low-resource language NLP","open-source NLP","pre-training instruction-tuning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-938A605423C4806B7CA2E68B0C70B68D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.80/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Northern European Association for Language Technology","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 25th Nordic Conference on Computational Lingustics and 11th Baltic Conference on Human Language Technologies : NoDaLiDa/Baltic-HLT 2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f723cc80-f5e3-4c09-996e-b1ba16b9c7f2","itu-bb98c006-6693-41e0-b20c-84f6825ba953"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"SnakModel : Lessons Learned from Training an Open Danish Large Language Model","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.89-813507","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Large Language Models (LLMs) have seen widespread societal adoption. However, while they are able to interact with users in languages beyond English, they have been shown to lack cultural awareness, providing anglocentric or inappropriate responses for underrepresented language communities. To investigate this gap and disentangle linguistic versus cultural proficiency, we conduct the first cultural evaluation study for the mid-resource language of Danish, in which native speakers prompt different models to solve tasks requiring cultural awareness. Our analysis of the resulting 1,038 interactions from 63 demographically diverse participants highlights open challenges to cultural adaptation: Particularly, how currently employed automatically translated data are insufficient to train or measure cultural adaptation, and how training on native-speaker data can more than double response acceptance rates. We release our study data as DaKultur - the first native Danish cultural awareness dataset.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Müller-Eberstein, Max","Zhang, Mike","Bassignana, Elisa","Brunsgaard Trolle, Peter","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S02-091.89-813317"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cultural Awareness","Danish language","Large Language Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dakultur evaluating the cultural awareness of language models for danish with native speakers","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.c3nlp-1.5/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.89-813317","ids":["aau-285c9042-fdc3-47f3-b49c-80a84514b36d","itu-39488485-b9dc-4aab-b098-1a00f4ad5114"],"keyword":["Cultural Awareness","DaKultur Dataset","Danish Language","Large Language Models","Native-Speaker Data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-CC65833422460DE272D3DF96AF29DBBB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.c3nlp-1.5/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"müllerebersteinpau","last":"Müller-Eberstein","locid":"523ffd96-f3b2-49cc-8f24-dc9215b84bed","name":"Müller-Eberstein, Max","orcid":"0000-0002-0006-0658","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"brunsgaardtrollepau","last":"Brunsgaard Trolle","name":"Brunsgaard Trolle, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brunsgaard","key":"trollepau","last":"Trolle","locid":"d21db1f2-9a89-4611-8077-e06e89985faa","name":"Trolle, Peter Brunsgaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"3rd Workshop on Cross-Cultural Considerations in NLP (C3NLP)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-285c9042-fdc3-47f3-b49c-80a84514b36d","itu-39488485-b9dc-4aab-b098-1a00f4ad5114"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DaKultur : Evaluating the Cultural Awareness of Language Models for Danish with Native Speakers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.89-813317","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Existing Large Multimodal Models (LMMs) generally focus on only a few regions and languages. As LMMs continue to improve, it is increasingly important to ensure they understand cultural contexts, respect local sensitivities, and support low-resource languages, all while effectively integrating corresponding visual cues. In pursuit of culturally diverse global multimodal models, our proposed All Languages Matter Benchmark (ALM-bench) represents the largest and most comprehensive effort to date for evaluating LMMs across 100 languages. ALM-bench challenges existing models by testing their ability to understand and reason about culturally diverse images paired with text in various languages, including many low-resource languages traditionally underrepresented in LMM research. The benchmark offers a robust and nuanced evaluation framework featuring various question formats, including true/false, multiple choice, and open-ended questions, which are further divided into short and long-answer categories. ALM-bench design ensures a comprehensive assessment of a model's ability to handle varied levels of difficulty in visual and linguistic reasoning. To capture the rich tapestry of global cultures, ALM-bench carefully curates content from 13 distinct cultural aspects, ranging from traditions and rituals to famous personalities and celebrations. Through this, ALM-bench not only provides a rigorous testing ground for state-of-the-art open and closed-source LMMs but also highlights the importance of cultural and linguistic inclusivity, encouraging the development of models that can serve diverse global populations effectively. Our benchmark is publicly available.","author_count":67,"contributors":["Vayani, Ashmal","Dissanayake, Dinura","Watawana, Hasindri","Ahsan, Noor","Sasikumar, Nevasini","Thawakar, Omkar","Ademtew, Henok Biadglign","Hmaiti, Yahya","Kumar, Amandeep","Kuckreja, Kartik","Maslych, Mykola","Ghallabi, Wafa Al","Qin, Chao","Shaker, Abdelrahman M","Zha