{"abstract":"This paper investigates whether Large Language Models (LLMs), fine-tuned on synthetic but domain-representative data, can perform the twofold task of (i) slot and intent detection and (ii) natural language response generation for a smart home assistant, while running solely on resource-limited, CPU-only edge hardware. We fine-tune LLMs to produce both JSON action calls and text responses. Our experiments show that 16-bit and 8-bit quantized variants preserve high accuracy on slot and intent detection and maintain strong semantic coherence in generated text, while the 4-bit model, while retaining generative fluency, suffers a noticeable drop in device-service classification accuracy. Further evaluations on noisy human (non-synthetic) prompts and out-of-domain intents confirm the models' generalization ability, obtaining around 80--86\\% accuracy. While the average inference time is 5--6 seconds per query -- acceptable for one-shot commands but suboptimal for multi-turn dialogue -- our results affirm that an on-device LLM can effectively unify command interpretation and flexible response generation for home automation without relying on specialized hardware.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Birkmose, Rune","Mørkeberg Reece, Nathan","Hofsted Norvin, Esben","Bjerva, Johannes","Zhang, Mike"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794269"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["LLM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on device llms for home assistant dual role in intent detection and response generation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.wnut-1.7/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-794269","ids":["aau-2b0a711e-c77a-4cae-bf28-0f17175e9607"],"keyword":["Home Assistant","LLM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-43C3AF1E0F92C3B332B59B1E2CB014F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.wnut-1.7/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.12923","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"birkmosepau","last":"Birkmose","name":"Birkmose, Rune","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nathan","key":"mørkebergreecepau","last":"Mørkeberg Reece","name":"Mørkeberg Reece, Nathan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben","key":"hofstednorvinpau","last":"Hofsted Norvin","name":"Hofsted Norvin, Esben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2502.12923","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Tenth Workshop on Noisy and User-generated Text (W-NUT 2025)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2b0a711e-c77a-4cae-bf28-0f17175e9607"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"On-Device LLMs for Home Assistant: Dual Role in Intent Detection and Response Generation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794269","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Large Language Models (LLMs) reproduce and exacerbate the social biases present in their training data, and resources to quantify this issue are limited. While research has attempted to identify and mitigate such biases, most efforts have been concentrated around English, lagging the rapid advancement of LLMs in multilingual settings. In this paper, we introduce a new multilingual parallel dataset SHADES to help address this issue, designed for examining culturally-specific stereotypes that may be learned by LLMs. The dataset includes stereotypes from 20 regions around the world and 16 languages, spanning multiple identity categories subject to discrimination worldwide. We demonstrate its utility in a series of exploratory evaluations for both “base” and “instruction-tuned” language models. Our results suggest that stereotypes are consistently reflected across models and languages, with some languages and models indicating much stronger stereotype biases than others.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ploeger, Esther","Zhang, Mike"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805383"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["BigScience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"shades towards a multilingual assessment of stereotypes in large language models","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-805383","ids":["aau-aee326f9-6cf7-4aec-9d90-1335feb90686"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F7210F894796C2D5C8F964AFD5683E9F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"bigscience","name":"BigScience","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esther","key":"ploegerpau","last":"Ploeger","locid":"0e27f320-d3de-49a4-b3af-1e35b2c1da53","name":"Ploeger, Esther","orcid":"0009-0007-9525-3359","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2025.naacl-long.600","pages":"11995-12041","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Conference of the Nations of the Americas Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Human Language Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aee326f9-6cf7-4aec-9d90-1335feb90686"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"SHADES: Towards a Multilingual Assessment of Stereotypes in Large Language Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805383","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Hackathons have become popular collaborative events for accelerating the development of creative ideas and prototypes. There are several case studies showcasing creative outcomes across domains such as industry, education, and research. However, there are no large-scale studies on creativity in hackathons which can advance theory on how hackathon formats lead to creative outcomes. We conducted a computational analysis of 193,353 hackathon projects. By operationalizing creativity through usefulness and novelty, we refined our dataset to 10,363 projects, allowing us to analyze how participant characteristics, collaboration patterns, and hackathon setups influence the development of creative projects. The contribution of our paper is twofold: We identified means for organizers to foster creativity in hackathons. We also explore the use of large language models (LLMs) to augment the evaluation of creative outcomes and discuss challenges and opportunities of doing this, which has implications for creativity research at large.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Falk, Jeanette","Chen, Yiyi","Rafner, Janet","Zhang, Mike","Bjerva, Johannes","Nolte, Alexander"],"cuid":["S02-091.00-813506"],"event":{"end":"2025-05-01","place":"Yokohama, jp","start":"2025-04-26","title":"2025 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems, CHI 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology"],"keyword":["Creativity","Hackathons","Human Centered AI","Large Language Models","Quantitative methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how do hackathons foster creativity towards automated evaluation of creativity at scale","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713447","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.00-813506","identifier":[{"id":"105005771402","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f68f9c82-3884-4c31-b847-1a8d76ea1690","au-69122028-66de-4e41-a29a-b19954eb0582"],"keyword":["Hackathons","creativity","human-centered AI","large language models","quantitative methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-657382922240615AADCC84080EAF2E3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3706598.3713447","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing","Aalborg University, [Mission] Improved Wellbeing Among Children And Youth In Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management","Aarhus University, Interfaculty Centre, Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeanette","key":"falkpau","last":"Falk","locid":"5084b27d-c3fe-43a4-9fe3-3ecd28908952","name":"Falk, Jeanette","orcid":"0000-0001-7278-9344","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yiyi","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"fac63374-6a8b-43fa-b74c-98b4c34fe64f","name":"Chen, Yiyi","orcid":"0000-0001-9977-8960","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janet","key":"rafnerpau","last":"Rafner","locid":"6eb09423-83bf-4190-94a5-a3f472891daa","name":"Rafner, Janet Frances","name_org":"Rafner, Janet","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-3334","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"noltepau","last":"Nolte","name":"Nolte, Alexander","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3706598.3713447","eisbn":["9798400713941"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2025 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","title":"CHI '25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005771402"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f68f9c82-3884-4c31-b847-1a8d76ea1690","au-69122028-66de-4e41-a29a-b19954eb0582"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How Do Hackathons Foster Creativity? Towards Automated Evaluation of Creativity at Scale","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.00-813506","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Matching job titles is a highly relevant task in the computational job market domain, as it improves e.g., automatic candidate matching, career path prediction, and job market analysis. Furthermore, aligning job titles to job skills can be considered an extension to this task, with similar relevance for the same downstream tasks. In this report, we outline NLPnorth's submission to TalentCLEF 2025, which includes both of these tasks: Multilingual Job Title Matching, and Job Title-Based Skill Prediction. For both tasks we compare (fine-tuned) classification-based, (fine-tuned) contrastive-based, and prompting methods. We observe that for Task A, our prompting approach performs best with an average of 0.492 mean average precision (MAP) on test data, averaged over English, Spanish, and German. For Task B, we obtain an MAP of 0.290 on test data with our fine-tuned classification-based approach. Additionally, we made use of extra data by pulling all the language-specific titles and corresponding \\emph{descriptions} from ESCO for each job and skill. Overall, we find that the largest multilingual language models perform best for both tasks. Per the provisional results and only counting the unique teams, the ranking on Task A is 5$^{\\text{th}}$/20 and for Task B 3$^{\\text{rd}}$/14.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823354"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs CL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nlpnorth talentclef 000000002025 comparing discriminative contrastive and prompt based methods for job title and skill matching","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790917596/2506.19058v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-823354","ids":["aau-3714efde-cbf9-4ff7-88ae-faf2620f499a"],"keyword":["cs.CL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-76B8B8CC0C3F18FC266BCC4A0638ED76"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/790917596/2506.19058v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","name":"van der Goot, Rob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3714efde-cbf9-4ff7-88ae-faf2620f499a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"NLPnorth @ TalentCLEF 2025 : Comparing Discriminative, Contrastive, and Prompt-Based Methods for Job Title and Skill Matching","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823354","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"End of semester student evaluations represent the primary feedback mechanism for academics' teaching practices. However, at the department or semester level, the sheer volume of feedback renders traditional analysis methods impractical. This paper addresses a gap in previous work where only course-level synthesis is explored using open-source generative AI for creating factual, actionable, and appropriate summaries of student feedback across an entire department. Instead, our study analyses 28 semester-level evaluation reports with student comments—with approximately 25,000 words and 170,000 characters—spanning the department, the model produces insights on several levels, namely degree-level, semester-level, year-level, and department-level. Through structured prompting, we developed a methodology that meets the specific needs of study board chairs who previously faced high workload from manually reviewing evaluations twice yearly. Our prompts allow the model to systematically checks for predetermined themes, while also identifying emergent patterns across courses. This approach enables targeted professional development initiatives at the departmental scale. Our contribution demonstrates that generative AI can effectively synthesize student feedback at a large organizational level, providing a cost-effective mechanism to support educational development and quality improvement across an entire academic unit.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Lindsay, Euan","Quitzau, Maj-Britt","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-804808"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scaling course evaluations with large language models semester level digestible student feedback for program leaders","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-804808","ids":["aau-2babc566-a803-4738-ac30-3e9ba612df14"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9C84B750675229530C1D1456E5E3433B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Euan","key":"lindsaypau","last":"Lindsay","locid":"3cd826f8-e16d-46cc-8b71-956ecaded5e5","name":"Lindsay, Euan","orcid":"0000-0003-3266-164X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maj-Britt","key":"quitzaupau","last":"Quitzau","locid":"97fc6821-a3f6-442b-ab49-3f4db6ee67e1","name":"Quitzau, Maj-Britt","orcid":"0000-0002-9907-8224","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"s"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-2babc566-a803-4738-ac30-3e9ba612df14"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Scaling Course Evaluations with Large Language Models: Semester-level Digestible Student Feedback for Program Leaders","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-804808","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The evaluation of vision-language models (VLMs) has mainly relied on English-language benchmarks, leaving significant gaps in both multilingual and multicultural coverage. While multilingual benchmarks have expanded, both in size and languages, many rely on translations of English datasets, failing to capture cultural nuances. In this work, we propose Kaleidoscope, as the most comprehensive exam benchmark to date for the multilingual evaluation of vision-language models. Kaleidoscope is a large-scale, in-language multimodal benchmark designed to evaluate VLMs across diverse languages and visual inputs. Kaleidoscope covers 18 languages and 14 different subjects, amounting to a total of 20,911 multiple-choice questions. Built through an open science collaboration with a diverse group of researchers worldwide, Kaleidoscope ensures linguistic and cultural authenticity. We evaluate top-performing multilingual vision-language models and find that they perform poorly on low-resource languages and in complex multimodal scenarios. Our results highlight the need for progress on culturally inclusive multimodal evaluation frameworks.","author_count":44,"contributors":["Salazar, Israfel","Burda, Manuel Fernández","Islam, Shayekh Bin","Moakhar, Arshia Soltani","Singh, Shivalika","Farestam, Fabian","Romanou, Angelika","Boiko, Danylo","Khullar, Dipika","Zhang, Mike","Krzemiński, Dominik","Novikova, Jekaterina","Shimabucoro, Luísa","Imperial, Joseph Marvin","Maheshwary, Rishabh","Duwal, Sharad","Amayuelas, Alfonso","Rajwal, Swati","Purbey, Jebish","Ruby, Ahmed","Popovič, Nicholas","Suppa, Marek","Wasi, Azmine Toushik","Kadiyala, Ram Mohan Rao","Tsymboi, Olga","Kostritsya, Maksim","Moakhar, Bardia Soltani","Merlin, Gabriel da Costa","Coletti, Otávio Ferracioli","Shiviari, Maral Jabbari","fard, MohammadAmin farahani","Fernandez, Silvia","Grandury, María","Abulkhanov, Dmitry","Sharma, Drishti","Mitri, Andre Guarnier De","Marchezi, Leticia Bossatto","Obando-Ceron, Johan","Kohut, Nazar","Ermis, Beyza","Elliott, Desmond","Ferrante, Enzo","Hooker, Sara","Fadaee, Marzieh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805174"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["cs CL","cs CV"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kaleidoscope in language exams for massively multilingual vision evaluation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-805174","ids":["aau-7c5a47ef-f5c9-488f-9585-dca33421eae0"],"keyword":["cs.CL","cs.CV"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-73C0CE7954D6E52930C1B65748A26612"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Israfel","key":"salazarisrafelpau","last":"Salazar","name":"Salazar, Israfel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Manuel Fernández","key":"burdamanuelfernándezpau","last":"Burda","name":"Burda, Manuel Fernández","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shayekh Bin","key":"islamshayekhbinpau","last":"Islam","name":"Islam, Shayekh Bin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Arshia Soltani","key":"moakhararshiasoltanipau","