{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianyu","key":"pangtianyupau","last":"Pang","name":"Pang, Tianyu","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Chao","key":"duchaopau","last":"Du","name":"Du, Chao","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinyi","key":"wanxinyipau","last":"Wan","name":"Wan, Xinyi","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Wei","key":"luweipau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Wei","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Min","key":"linminpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Min","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"u"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Unpublished"]},"sid":["aau-850d43b2-b97a-47fe-a15a-48fd804afe15"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sailor2: Sailing in South-East Asia with Inclusive Multilingual LLMs","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794759","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Providing high-quality feedback is crucial for student success but is constrained by time, cost, and limited data availability. We introduce Synthetic Educational Feedback Loops (SEFL), a novel framework designed to deliver immediate, on-demand feedback at scale without relying on extensive, real-world student data. In SEFL, two large language models (LLMs) operate in teacher--student roles to simulate assignment completion and formative feedback, generating abundant synthetic pairs of student work and corresponding critiques. We then fine-tune smaller, more computationally efficient LLMs on these synthetic pairs, enabling them to replicate key features of high-quality, goal-oriented feedback. Unlike personalized tutoring approaches that offer multi-turn, individualized instruction, SEFL specifically focuses on replicating the teacher-->student feedback loop for diverse assignments. Through both LLM-as-a-judge and human evaluations, we demonstrate that SEFL-tuned models outperform their non-tuned counterparts in feedback quality, clarity, and timeliness. These findings reveal SEFL's potential to transform feedback processes for higher education and beyond, offering an ethical and scalable alternative to conventional manual feedback cycles.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Dilling, Amalie Pernille","Gondelman, Léon","Lyngdorf, Niels Erik Ruan","Lindsay, Euan","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-795092"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["LLM","NLP"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sefl harnessing large language model agents to improve educational feedback systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-795092","ids":["aau-c570da63-bc36-4f6a-80ed-159c03c1e076"],"keyword":["Automated Feedback","LLM","LLM-as-a-judge","NLP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7D797C6347D89FC519B07F7C8D51A434"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Amalie Pernille","key":"dillingpau","last":"Dilling","locid":"440d5a10-a0da-4165-bb1b-a8e733fb828d","name":"Dilling, Amalie Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Léon","key":"gondelmanpau","last":"Gondelman","locid":"2927c533-0b75-4347-a6a8-b3c8d47059cc","name":"Gondelman, Léon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Erik","key":"lyngdorfpau","last":"Lyngdorf","locid":"1d727480-b5f2-4a47-8793-2cb1e167c47f","name":"Lyngdorf, Niels Erik Ruan","name_org":"Lyngdorf, Niels Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8737-0044","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Euan","key":"lindsaypau","last":"Lindsay","locid":"3cd826f8-e16d-46cc-8b71-956ecaded5e5","name":"Lindsay, Euan","orcid":"0000-0003-3266-164X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2502.12927","status":"s"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-c570da63-bc36-4f6a-80ed-159c03c1e076"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"SEFL: Harnessing Large Language Model Agents to Improve Educational Feedback Systems","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-795092","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Current language models (LMs) mostly exploit subwords as input units based on statistical co-occurrences of characters. Adjacently, previous work has shown that modeling morphemes can aid performance for Natural Language Processing (NLP) models. However, morphemes are challenging to obtain as there is no annotated data in most languages. In this work, we release a wide-coverage Danish morphological segmentation evaluation set. We evaluate a wide variety of unsupervised token segmenters and evaluate the downstream effect of using morphemes as input units for transformer-based LMs. Our results show that popular subword algorithms perform poorly on this task, scoring at most an $F_1$ of 44.8 compared to 58.6 for an unsupervised morphological segmented (Morfessor). Furthermore, we confirm that the more closely our tokenizer resembles morphemes, the higher the performance of LMs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["van der Goot, Rob","Jensen, Anette","Allerslev Schledermann, Emil","Wildner Kildeberg, Mikkel","Larsen, Nicolaj","Zhang, Mike","Bassignana, Elisa"],"cuid":["S02-083.61-822464"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Danish language processing","Morphological segmentation","Transformer based language models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"morsed morphological segmentation of danish and its effect on language modeling","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.61-822464","ids":["aau-cdd51d4a-0153-4cd6-b5ca-2c7f2c97e306","itu-a4555d83-5f29-4b04-b0c3-13151f26d4c8"],"keyword":["Danish language processing","Morpheme-based input representations","Morphological segmentation","Transformer-based language models","Unsupervised token segmentation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-321607212045F25CBC149346C9489375"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2025.nodalida-1.23.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob van der","key":"gootpau","last":"Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","name_org":"Goot, Rob van der","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Anette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Allerslev","key":"schledermannpau","last":"Schledermann","name":"Schledermann, Emil Allerslev","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Wildner","key":"kildebergpau","last":"Kildeberg","name":"Kildeberg, Mikkel Wildner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolaj","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Nicolaj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisa","key":"bassignanapau","last":"Bassignana","locid":"c6b67626-5ff8-4730-93a6-70ee08f6013e","name":"Bassignana, Elisa","orcid":"0009-0003-8374-7571","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard","key":"johanssonpedh","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Richard","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sara","key":"stymnepedh","last":"Stymne","name":"Stymne, Sara","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789908531090"],"pages":"223-229","place":"Tallinn, Estonia","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Joint 25th Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics and 11th Baltic Conference on Human Language Technologies (NoDaLiDa/Baltic-HLT 2025)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cdd51d4a-0153-4cd6-b5ca-2c7f2c97e306","itu-a4555d83-5f29-4b04-b0c3-13151f26d4c8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MorSeD : Morphological Segmentation of Danish and its Effect on Language Modeling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.61-822464","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The performance differential of large language models (LLM) between languages hinders their effective deployment in many regions, inhibiting the potential economic and societal value of generative AI tools in many communities. However, the development of functional LLMs in many languages (\\ie, multilingual LLMs) is bottlenecked by the lack of high-quality evaluation resources in languages other than English. Moreover, current practices in multilingual benchmark construction often translate English resources, ignoring the regional and cultural knowledge of the environments in which multilingual systems would be used. In this work, we construct an evaluation suite of 197,243 QA pairs from local exam sources to measure the capabilities of multilingual LLMs in a variety of regional contexts. Our novel resource, INCLUDE, is a comprehensive knowledge- and reasoning-centric benchmark across 44 written languages that evaluates multilingual LLMs for performance in the actual language environments where they would be deployed.","author_count":59,"contributors":["Romanou, Angelika","Foroutan, Negar","Sotnikova, Anna","Chen, Zeming","Nelaturu, Sree Harsha","Singh, Shivalika","Maheshwary, Rishabh","Altomare, Micol","Haggag, Mohamed A.","Snegha, A","Amayuelas, Alfonso","Amirudin, Azril Hafizi","Aryabumi, Viraat","Boiko, Danylo","Chang, Michael","Chim, Jenny","Cohen, Gal","Dalmia, Aditya Kumar","Diress, Abraham","Duwal, Sharad","Dzenhaliou, Daniil","Florez, Daniel Fernando Erazo","Farestam, Fabian","Imperial, Joseph Marvin","Islam, Shayekh Bin","Isotalo, Perttu","Jabbarishiviari, Maral","Karlsson, Börje F.","Khalilov, Eldar","Klamm, Christopher","Koto, Fajri","Krzemiński, Dominik","de Melo, Gabriel Adriano","Montariol, Syrielle","Nan, Yiyang","Niklaus, Joel","Novikova, Jekaterina","Ceron, Johan Samir Obando","Paul, Debjit","Ploeger, Esther","Purbey, Jebish","Rajwal, Swati","Ravi, Selvan Sunitha","Rydell, Sara","Santhosh, Roshan","Sharma, Drishti","Skenduli, Marjana P