{"abstract":"Recent approaches in skill-to-surface-form matching, employing synthetic training data for classification or similarity model training, have shown promising results, eliminating the need for time-consuming and expensive annotation. However, previous datasets have limitations, such as featuring only one skill per sentence and generally comprising short sentences. This paper introduces JobSkape, a framework to generate synthetic data that resembles real-world job postings, specifically designed to enhance skill-to-taxonomy matching. Within this framework, we create SkillSkape, a comprehensive open-source synthetic dataset of job postings tailored for skill-matching tasks. We introduce several offline metrics that show our dataset is more diverse, realistic, and follows a higher quality based on similarities. Additionally, we present a multi-step pipeline utilizing large language models (LLMs), benchmarking against supervised methodologies. We outline that the performances are comparable and that each method can be used for different use cases.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Magron, Antoine","Dai, Anna","Zhang, Mike","Montariol, Syrielle","Bosselut, Antoine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730175"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne"],"keyword":["Job postings","Large Language Models LLMs","Skill matching tasks","Skill to surface form matching","Synthetic training data"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jobskape a framework for generating synthetic job postings to enhance skill matching","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730175","ids":["itu-69f7a6f5-a1f3-4157-bad0-1da73afca296"],"keyword":["Job postings","Large language models (LLMs)","Skill-matching tasks","Skill-to-surface-form matching","Synthetic training data"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D974B9EBEB742DCE3D1090ECC336ACBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.4/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"ecole polytechnique fédérale de lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoine","key":"magronpau","last":"Magron","name":"Magron, Antoine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"daipau","last":"Dai","name":"Dai, Anna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Syrielle","key":"montariolpau","last":"Montariol","name":"Montariol, Syrielle","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoine","key":"bosselutpau","last":"Bosselut","name":"Bosselut, Antoine","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"43-58","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"1st Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Human Resources"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69f7a6f5-a1f3-4157-bad0-1da73afca296"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"JobSkape: A Framework for Generating Synthetic Job Postings to Enhance Skill Matching","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730175","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The I-DIFFER project aimed to develop and demonstrate a novel, and easily implementable renovation solution that can enhance overall indoor environmental quality in buildings, specifically addressing improvements in air quality, thermal comfort, and acoustics. The project introduces the I-DIFFER solution, which integrates technologies such as the Double Skin Facade (DSF), Diffuse Ceiling Ventilation (DCV), and a ventilation control system. This solution employs a mechanical exhaust system, transporting fresh air through the DSF into the diffuse ceiling plenum and then into the occupied space to ensure satisfactory indoor conditions. The I-DIFFER project evolved through simulation testing, establishing the fundamental concept of integrating the above-mentioned technologies. The energy performance and comfort were assessed across several scenarios, including variations in the outer layer of DSF, building orientation, etc. Subsequently, the I-DIFFER solution prototype was selected, and evaluated experimentally in a full-scale outdoor façade laboratory. This step was to verify the efficiency of the developed solution in ensuring a high environmental quality and avoiding the potential risks (draught and overheating). An optimized I-DIFFER solution was then implemented at the Ellehøjskolen classroom for demonstration. Performance assessment in the demonstration building revealed positive outcomes, including superior air quality, good thermal comfort and strong indications of energy efficiency of the solution.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Olena Kalyanova","Zhang, Chen","Thomsen Nielsen, Lars","Madsen, Mike Vinge","Brøchner Bække, Sara","Tranholm, Gitte Thorup","Thomsen, Ulrik","Kappel, Niels","Atzen, Bent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752543"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diffuse ceiling ventilation","Double Skin Facade","Experimental testing"],"level":"pop","mr