nternational Conference on Computational Linguistics, Language Resources and Evaluation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5e6d8889-8e32-4cb4-a124-5b106698df8a","itu-5671851b-0bf7-4b68-86b0-0e1120971c10"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Can Humans Identify Domains?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.66-741398","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Recent years have brought significant advances to Natural Language Processing (NLP), which enabled fast progress in the field of computational job market analysis. Core tasks in this application domain are skill extraction and classification from job postings. Because of its quick growth and its interdisciplinary nature, there is no exhaustive assessment of this field. This survey aims to fill this gap by providing a comprehensive overview of deep learning methodologies, datasets, and terminologies specific to NLP-driven skill extraction. Our comprehensive cataloging of publicly available datasets addresses the lack of consolidated information on dataset creation and characteristics. Finally, the focus on terminology addresses the current lack of consistent definitions for important concepts, such as hard and soft skills, and terms relating to skill extraction and classification.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Senger, Elena","Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730191"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich"],"keyword":["Deep Learning Methodologies","Job Market Analysis","Natural Language Processing NLP","Public Datasets","Skill Extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep learning based computational job market analysis a survey on skill extraction and classification from job postings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730191","ids":["itu-c29161fe-e38e-4086-b98a-cba9a4eefd88"],"keyword":["Deep Learning Methodologies","Job Market Analysis","Natural Language Processing (NLP)","Public Datasets","Skill Extraction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BB4DA2D1ED6BE5DC5E41DC7A0589DC0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.1/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"sengerpau","last":"Senger","name":"Senger, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1-15","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"1st Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Human Resources"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c29161fe-e38e-4086-b98a-cba9a4eefd88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Learning-based Computational Job Market Analysis: A Survey on Skill Extraction and Classification from Job Postings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730191","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"End of semester student evaluations of teaching are the dominant mechanism for providing feedback to academics on their teaching practice. For large classes, however, the volume of feedback makes these tools impractical for this purpose. This paper explores the use of open-source generative AI to synthesise factual, actionable and appropriate summaries of student feedback from these survey responses. In our setup, we have 742 student responses ranging over 75 courses in a Computer Science department. For each course, we synthesise a summary of the course evaluations and actionable items for the instructor. Our results reveal a promising avenue for enhancing teaching practices in the classroom setting. Our contribution lies in demonstrating the feasibility of using generative AI to produce insightful feedback for teachers, thus providing a cost-effective means to support educators' development. Overall, our work highlights the possibility of using generative AI to produce factual, actionable, and appropriate feedback for teachers in the classroom setting.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Lindsay, Euan","Thorbensen, Frederik Bode","Poulsen, Danny Bøgsted","Bjerva, Johannes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-742590"],"event":{"end":"2024-09-05","place":"Lausanne, ch","start":"2024-09-02","title":"SEFI 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Lindsay, Euan"],"keyword":["AI in Education","Education","Large Language Model","Natural Language Processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leveraging large language models for actionable course evaluation student feedback to lecturers","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/756472836/226_Zhang-Leveraging_Large_Language_Models_for_Actionable_Course_Evaluation_Student_Feedback-347_paper.pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-742590","identifier":[{"id":"85218632594","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-19b02384-b88f-4404-b0a2-f5d5eec1207f"],"keyword":["AI in Education","Education","Large Language Model","Natural Language Processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-14BD5174973CD219455C169BA4C155CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2407.01274","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/756472836/226_Zhang-Leveraging_Large_Language_Models_for_Actionable_Course_Evaluation_Student_Feedback-347_paper.pdf.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/766365594/b_226_Zhang-Leveraging_Large_Language_Models_for_Actionable_Course_Evaluation_Student_Feedback-347_paper.pdf.pdf_","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://zenodo.org/records/14254832","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Data, Knowledge and Web Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"95b88f39-4927-48b0-9415-b2b3d0b43db8","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Euan","key":"lindsaypau","last":"Lindsay","locid":"3cd826f8-e16d-46cc-8b71-956ecaded5e5","name":"Lindsay, Euan","orcid":"0000-0003-3266-164X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Bode","key":"thorbensenpau","last":"Thorbensen","locid":"52f12262-7510-472b-8940-ad5b7cab175c","name":"Thorbensen, Frederik Bode","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Danny Bøgsted","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"dfb3337d-6acd-49e8-a38c-d819a6efca6c","name":"Poulsen, Danny Bøgsted","orcid":"0000-0001-9623-0748","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johannes","key":"bjervapau","last":"Bjerva","locid":"67f84fc4-668e-4249-8782-09b037a44fd4","name":"Bjerva, Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-9512-0739","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2407.01274","eisbn":["9782873520274"],"pages":"1089-1098","publisher":"Société européenne pour la formation des ingénieurs (SEFI)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 52nd Annual Conference of the European Society for Engineering Education (SEFI)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218632594"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-19b02384-b88f-4404-b0a2-f5d5eec1207f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Leveraging Large Language Models for Actionable Course Evaluation Student Feedback to Lecturers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-742590","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The labor market is changing rapidly, prompting increased interest in the automatic extraction of occupational skills from text. With the advent of English benchmark job description datasets, there is a need for systems that handle their diversity well. We tackle the complexity in occupational skill datasets tasks---combining and leveraging multiple datasets for skill extraction, to identify rarely observed skills within a dataset, and overcoming the scarcity of skills across datasets. In particular, we investigate the retrieval-augmentation of language models, employing an external datastore for retrieving similar skills in a dataset-unifying manner. Our proposed method, Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction (NNOSE) effectively leverages multiple datasets by retrieving neighboring skills from other datasets in the datastore. This improves skill extraction without additional fine-tuning. Crucially, we observe a performance gain in predicting infrequent patterns, with substantial gains of up to 30% span-F1 in cross-dataset settings.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Kan, Min-Yen","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730163"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National University of Singapore"],"keyword":["Benchmark job description datasets","Labor market","Language Models","Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction NNOSE","Occupational skills extraction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nnose nearest neighbor occupational skill extraction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730163","ids":["itu-2a506ba1-33c4-4015-bd87-ce515688f65b"],"keyword":["Benchmark job description datasets","Labor market","Language models","Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction (NNOSE)","Occupational skills extraction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F0044AD8DC15DC05BAB3DBF221A38DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.eacl-long.35/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"national university of singapore","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"National University of Singapore","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Min-Yen","key":"kanpau","last":"Kan","name":"Kan, Min-Yen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"589-608","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"The 18th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2a506ba1-33c4-4015-bd87-ce515688f65b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"NNOSE: Nearest Neighbor Occupational Skill Extraction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730163","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Recent technological advances underscore the dynamic nature of the labor market. These transformative shifts yield significant consequences for employment prospects, resulting in the increase of job vacancy data across platforms and languages. The aggregation of such data holds the potential to gain valuable insights into labor market demands, the emergence of new skills, and the overall facilitation of job matching. These benefits extend to various parties, including job platforms, recruitment agencies, applicants, and other stakeholders within the ecosystem. However, despite the prevalence of such insights in the private sector, we lack transparent language technology systems and data for this domain. The primary objective of this thesis is to investigate the use of Natural Language Processing (NLP) technology for the extraction of relevant information from job descriptions. We identify several general challenges within this domain. These encompass a scarcity of available training and evaluation data, a lack of standardized guidelines to annotate data, and a shortage of effective methods for extracting information from job ads. Therefore, we embark on a comprehensive study of the entire process: First, framing the problem and getting annotated data for training NLP models. Here, our contributions encompass job description datasets, including a de-identification dataset, and a novel active learning algorithm designed for efficient model training. Second, we introduce several extraction methodologies to tackle the task of information extraction from job advertisement data: A skill extraction approach using weak supervision, a taxonomy-aware pre-training methodology adapting a multilingual language model to the job market domain, and a retrieval-augmented model leveraging multiple skill extraction datasets to enhance overall extraction performance. Lastly, given the extracted information, we delve into the grounding of this data within a designated taxonomy.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730168"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational job market analysis with natural language processing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068611/phd-thesis-final_version_Mike_Zhang.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730168","ids":["itu-547e19a2-a61b-45ca-99c6-04568cb78b86"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3CCD6CDD9CD88F29FBBB75687E6C9A1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/109068611/phd-thesis-final_version_Mike_Zhang.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788779494145"],"pages":"314","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-547e19a2-a61b-45ca-99c6-04568cb78b86"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computational Job Market Analysis : with Natural Language Processing","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730168","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Skill Extraction involves identifying skills and qualifications mentioned in documents such as job postings and resumes. It is commonly tackled by training supervised models using a sequence labeling approach with BIO tags. However, the reliance on manually annotated data limits the generalizability of such approaches. Moreover, the common BIO setting limits the ability of the models to capture complex skill patterns and handle ambiguous mentions. In this paper, we explore the use of in-context learning to overcome these challenges, on a benchmark of 6 skill extraction datasets that we uniformize. Our approach leverages the few-shot learning capabilities of large language models (LLMs) to identify and extract skills from sentences. We show that LLMs, despite not being on par with traditional supervised models in terms of performance, can better handle syntactically complex skill mentions in skill extraction tasks.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nguyen, Khanh Cao","Zhang, Mike","Montariol, Syrielle","Bosselut, Antoine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730203"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne"],"keyword":["BIO Tags","Few Shot Learning","In Context Learning","Skill Extraction","Supervised Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rethinking skill extraction in the job market domain using large language models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730203","ids":["itu-f0766913-f2b9-4940-8362-a8156f720345"],"keyword":["BIO Tags","Few-Shot Learning","In-Context Learning","Skill Extraction","Supervised Models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B7CAE63105819F94E55B55C0B4811D0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.3/","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.nlp4hr-1.3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"ecole polytechnique fédérale de lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Ecole Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Khanh Cao","key":"nguyenpau","last":"Nguyen","name":"Nguyen, Khanh Cao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Syrielle","key":"montariolpau","last":"Montariol","name":"Montariol, Syrielle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antoine","key":"bosselutpau","last":"Bosselut","name":"Bosselut, Antoine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"27-42","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"1st Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Human Resources"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f0766913-f2b9-4940-8362-a8156f720345"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rethinking Skill Extraction in the Job Market Domain using Large Language Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730203","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In Natural Language Processing, entity linking (EL) has centered around Wikipedia, but yet remains underexplored for the job market domain. Disambiguating skill mentions can help us get insight into the current labor market demands. In this work, we are the first to explore EL in this domain, specifically targeting the linkage of occupational skills to the ESCO taxonomy (le Vrang et al., 2014). Previous efforts linked coarse-grained (full) sentences to a corresponding ESCO skill. In this work, we link more fine-grained span-level mentions of skills. We tune two high-performing neural EL models, a bi-encoder (Wu et al., 2020) and an autoregressive model (Cao et al., 2021), on a synthetically generated mention–skill pair dataset and evaluate them on a human-annotated skill-linking benchmark. Our findings reveal that both models are capable of linking implicit mentions of skills to their correct taxonomy counterparts. Empirically, BLINK outperforms GENRE in strict evaluation, but GENRE performs better in loose evaluation (accuracy@k).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","van der Goot, Rob","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730204"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ESCO Taxonomy","Entity Linking","Natural Language Processing","Neural models","Occupational Skills"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"entity linking in the job market domain","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730204","ids":["itu-f13178df-cafe-4855-86ee-f18db7fc8afa"],"keyword":["ESCO Taxonomy","Entity Linking","Natural Language Processing","Neural Models","Occupational Skills"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-84C3025A24589417B7A4C7C62C7964B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-eacl.28/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"vandergootpau","last":"van der Goot","locid":"8e5f2a6c-c817-4a90-b48b-d9171743ad0f","name":"van der Goot, Rob","orcid":"0009-0003-1999-4156","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"410-419","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"The 18th Conference of the European Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f13178df-cafe-4855-86ee-f18db7fc8afa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Entity Linking in the Job Market Domain","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730204","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The I-DIFFER is the novel approach to renovate buildings quickly and subtly, particularly those like schools and offices with high internal heat load and ventilation needs. The I-DIFFER principle combines Double-Skin Façade (DSF) and Diffuse Ceiling (DC) ventilation using smart controls. This guide aims to offer insights into key considerations for planning, designing, constructing, and operating I-DIFFER solution. In addition, the guide aims to inspire the adoption of the I-DIFFER solution in other projects. Whether you're an architect, engineer, or building manager, this document will support you in successful implementation of the I-DIFFER approach to improve energy efficiency, comfort and sustainability in your project. The advices provided in this guide are rooted in practical experiences drawn from the I-DIFFER project and the collective wisdom of project partners. It is important for the reader to bear in mind that these recommendations are based on a limited number of cases. Thus, a careful consideration of the specific context and needs of your project must not be forgotten. For more information, please refer to publications, reports and guidelines included in the list of references. The I-DIFFER project has received funding from the Energy Technology Development and Demonstration Program (EUDP), Denmark, under the name I-DIFFER (Journal number: 64020-2140).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Larsen, Olena Kalyanova","Zhang, Chen","Thomsen Nielsen, Lars","Vinge Madsen, Mike","Brøchner Bække, Sara","Thorup Tranhom, Gitte","Thomsen, Ulrik","Kappel, Niels","Atzen, Bent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752000"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Aarhus Kommune"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design guide for i differ the double skin facade solution with integrated diffuse ventilation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/732915044/I-DIFFER_WP5_Design_guide.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Energy Technology Development and Demonstration Program (EUDP) under the name I- DIFFER (Journal number: 64 020–2140), Denmark."],"id":"S01-000.00-752000","ids":["aau-0f8f7277-04a0-4cf0-8c9b-01d505260232"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F5AAED0673CA929E53B28C19E2C4D684"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/732915044/I-DIFFER_WP5_Design_guide.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Architectural Engineering","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Energy and Buildings Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Aarhus Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Othe