{"abstract":"De-identification is the task of detecting privacy-related entities in text, such as person names, emails and contact data. It has been well-studied within the medical domain. The need for de-identification technology is increasing, as privacy-preserving data handling is in high demand in many domains. In this paper, we focus on job postings. We present JobStack, a new corpus for de-identification of personal data in job vacancies on Stackoverflow. We introduce baselines, comparing Long-Short Term Memory (LSTM) and Transformer models. To improve upon these baselines, we experiment with contextualized embeddings and distantly related auxiliary data via multi-task learning. Our results show that auxiliary data improves de-identification performance.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","Zhang, Mike","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382435"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Baselines","De identification","Job postings","JobStack corpus","Long short term memory LSTM","Medical domain","Personal data","Privacy preserving data","Privacy related entities","Transformer models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de identification of privacy related entities in job postings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85880206/JobStack_NoDaLiDa_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382435","ids":["itu-4e400a88-6fcb-4ba1-ae10-675b004fd96f"],"keyword":["Baselines","De-identification","Job postings","JobStack corpus","Long-Short Term Memory (LSTM)","Medical domain","Personal data","Privacy-preserving data","Privacy-related entities","Transformer models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A318D3CE2066B5BFD8857202C992945A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85880206/JobStack_NoDaLiDa_2021.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Nørgaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"04344edd-2f02-45d5-ad45-baffe4c08898","name":"Jensen, Kristian Nørgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"21","pages":"210-221","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","series":"Linköping Electronic Conference Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 23rd Nordic Conference on Computational Linguistics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4e400a88-6fcb-4ba1-ae10-675b004fd96f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"De-identification of Privacy-related Entities in Job Postings","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382435","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We propose Cartography Active Learning (CAL), a novel Active Learning (AL) algorithm that exploits the behavior of the model on individual instances during training as a proxy to find the most informative instances for labeling. CAL is inspired by data maps, which were recently proposed to derive insights into dataset quality (Swayamdipta et al., 2020). We compare our method on popular text classification tasks to commonly used AL strategies, which instead rely on post-training behavior. We demonstrate that CAL is competitive to other common AL methods, showing that training dynamics derived from small seed data can be successfully used for AL. We provide insights into our new AL method by analyzing batch-level statistics utilizing the data maps. Our results further show that CAL results in a more data-efficient learning strategy, achieving comparable or better results with considerably less training data.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Zhang, Mike","Plank, Barbara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383635"],"event":{"acronym":"EMNLP","title":"Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Cartography Active Learning","Data Efficiency","Text classification","Training Dynamics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cartography active learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.findings-emnlp.36","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383635","identifier":[{"id":"85121620236","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a27ef98e-b998-4b5f-a8cd-df71fd254033"],"keyword":["Active Learning","Cartography Active Learning","Data Efficiency","Text Classification","Training Dynamics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C7C7FE5154A45A490BAE3B97BB5C66B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2021.findings-emnlp.36","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86349956/2021.findings_emnlp.36.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2021.findings-emnlp.36.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NLPnorth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","locid":"78a992d3-b8eb-4fd6-8a5e-18c464d0b254","name":"Zhang, Mike","orcid":"0000-0003-1218-5201","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Barbara","key":"plankpau","last":"Plank","locid":"f073ebac-704d-4236-9206-d1d2ef2be9c3","name":"Plank, Barbara","orcid":"0000-0002-4394-1965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18653/v1/2021.findings-emnlp.36","pages":"395-406","publisher":"Association for Computational Linguistics","status":"p","title":"Findings of the Association for Computational Linguistics: EMNLP 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121620236"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a27ef98e-b998-4b5f-a8cd-df71fd254033"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cartography Active Learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383635","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Reported COVID-19 deaths in Germany are relatively low as compared to many European countries. Among the several explanations proposed, an early and large testing of the population was put forward. Most current debates on COVID-19 focus on the differences among countries, but little attention has been given to regional differences and diet. The low-death rate European countries (e.g. Austria, Baltic States, Czech Republic, Finland, Norway, Poland, Slovakia) have used different quarantine and/or confinement times and methods and none have performed as many early tests as Germany. Among other factors that may be significant are the dietary habits. It seems that some foods largely used in these countries may reduce angiotensin-converting enzyme activity or are anti-oxidants. Among the many possible areas of research, it might be important to understand diet and angiotensin-converting enzyme-2 (ACE2) levels in populations with different COVID-19 death rates since dietary interventions may be of great benefit.","author_count":581,"contributors":["Bousquet, Jean","Anto, Josep M.","Iaccarino, Guido","Czarlewski, Wienczyslawa","Haahtela, Tari","Anto, Aram","Akdis, Cezmi","Blain, Hubert","Canonica, G. Walter","Cardona, Victoria","Cruz, Alvaro A.","Illario, Maddalena","Ivancevich, Juan Carlos","Jutel, Marek","Klimek, Ludger","Kuna, Piotr","Laune, Daniel","Larenas-linnemann, Désirée","Mullol, Joaquim","Papadopoulos, Nikos G.","Pfaar, Oliver","Samolinski, Boleslaw","Valiulis, Arunas","Yorgancioglu, Arzu","Zuberbier, Torsten","Latiff, Amir","Abdullah, Baharudin","Aberer, Werner","Abusada, Nancy","Adcock, Ian","Afani, Alejandro","Agache, Ioana","Aggelidis, Xenofon","Agustin, Jenifer","Akdis, Cezmi","Akdis, Mübeccel","Al-Ahmad, Mona","Bassam, Abou Al Zahab","Aldrey-Palacios, Oscar","Cuesta, Emilio Alvarez","Alzaabi, Ashraf","Amad, Salma","Ambrocio, Gene","Annesi-Maesano, Isabella","Ansotegui, Ignacio","Anto, Josep","Arshad, Hasan","Artesani, Maria Cristina","Asayag, E