{"abstract":"The papers in this special section examine the enabling of very high penetration renewable energy integration into future power systems. Renewable energy is regarded as one of the main solutions to achieve power system sustainability. In recent years, renewable energy has been experiencing fast development. In 2016, 24.5% of the total power demand in the world was supplied by renewable energy, where 5.5% was produced by wind power and PV [item 1) in the Appendix]. It is estimated that by the end of 2017 the global wind power and PV capacity had reached about 565 GW and 335 GW respectively. Some power systems have already entered the era of high penetration of intermittent renewable energy integration.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kang, Chongqing","Chen, Zhe","Zhang, Ning","Gomis-Bellmunt, Oriol","Barnes, Mike","Yan, Jie","Hu, Weihao","Sun, Kai"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123573"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Spain","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","North China Electric Power University","Polytechnic University of Catalonia","Tsinghua University","University of Manchester","University of Tennessee, Knoxville"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guest editorial for the special section on enabling very high penetration renewable energy integration into future power systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dje","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85046008555&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Different countries increasingly support projects in the research of high penetration renewable energy integration. Such as series studies at National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL) supported by Department of Energy in US, the research and innovation programme H2020 in European Union, and series of high penetration renewable energy projects in National Key Research and Development (R&D) Program of China. In 2016, the National Key R&D Program of China approved a project entitled Fundamental Theory of Planning and Operation for Power Systems with High Share of Renewable Energy Generations (under grant No. 2016YFB0900100). The overall objective of this project is to study the basic theory and method of planning and operation of high penetration renewable energy power systems and to provide standardized systems for a high share of renewable energy integration."],"id":"S01-000.00-123573","identifier":[{"id":"85046008555","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fd3c6118-b733-475c-aa51-17e9775c14fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F0E5E8E32CC64A60B20BC2532D586F3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"tsinghua university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Tsinghua University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, AAU Energy, Electric Power Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"es","key":"polytechnic university of catalonia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Catalonia","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of manchester","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Manchester","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"north china electric power university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"North China Electric Power University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"university of tennessee knoxville","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Tennessee, Knoxville","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chongqing","key":"kangpau","last":"Kang","name":"Kang, Chongqing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Zhe","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","locid":"d823b80a-ad7f-4339-b75a-8dee8403f02a","name":"Chen, Zhe","orcid":"0000-0002-2919-4481","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ning","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Oriol","key":"gomisbellmuntpau","last":"Gomis-Bellmunt","name":"Gomis-Bellmunt, Oriol","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"barnespau","last":"Barnes","name":"Barnes, Mike","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jie","key":"yanpau","last":"Yan","name":"Yan, Jie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Weihao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","locid":"6a8d73a0-43d8-4b65-a4d0-4f62e2cc4315","name":"Hu, Weihao","orcid":"0000-0003-3816-7263","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Kai","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tpwrs.2018.2819738","issn":["08858950"],"issue":"3","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Power Systems","pages":"3223-3226","publisher":"IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Power Systems","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046008555"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fd3c6118-b733-475c-aa51-17e9775c14fb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Guest Editorial for the Special Section on Enabling Very High Penetration Renewable Energy Integration into Future Power Systems","type":"Editorial","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123573","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Nomenclatural type definitions are one of the most important concepts in biological nomenclature. Being physical objects that can be re-studied by other researchers, types permanently link taxonomy (an artificial agreement to classify biological diversity) with nomenclature (an artificial agreement to name biological diversity). Two proposals to amend the International Code of Nomenclature for algae, fungi, and plants (ICN), allowing DNA sequences alone (of any region and extent) to serve as types of taxon names for voucherless fungi (mainly putative taxa from environmental DNA sequences), have been submitted to be voted on at the 11th International Mycological Congress (Puerto Rico, July 2018). We consider various genetic processes affecting the distribution of alleles among taxa and find that alleles may not consistently and uniquely represent the species within which they are contained. Should the proposals be accepted, the meaning of nomenclatural types would change in a fundamental way from physical objects as sources of data to the data themselves. Such changes are conducive to irreproducible science, the potential typification on artefactual data, and massive creation of names with low information content, ultimately causing nomenclatural instability and unnecessary work for future researchers that would stall future explorations of fungal diversity. We conclude that the acceptance of DNA sequences alone as types of names of taxa, under the terms used in the current proposals, is unnecessary and would not solve the problem of naming putative taxa known only from DNA sequences in a scientifically defensible way. As an alternative, we highlight the use of formulas for naming putative taxa (candidate taxa) that do not require any modification of the ICN.","author_count":412,"contributors":["Zamora, Juan Carlos","Svensson, Mans","Kirschner, Roland","Olariaga, Ibai","Ryman, Svengunnar","Alberto Parra, Luis","Geml, Jozsef","Rosling, Anna","Adamcik, Sla