,"DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a74a1dc0-53b6-4b2b-9e7b-4235286dd94b","ku-19a49266-3069-454c-8d17-5432759140f5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PESFOR-W: Improving the design and environmental effectiveness of woodlands for water Payments for Ecosystem Services","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.73-024896","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Cardiac arrhythmias and conduction disturbances are accompanied by structural remodelling of the specialised cardiomyocytes known collectively as the cardiac conduction system. Here, using contrast enhanced micro-computed tomography, we present, in attitudinally appropriate fashion, the first 3-dimensional representations of the cardiac conduction system within the intact human heart. We show that cardiomyocyte orientation can be extracted from these datasets at spatial resolutions approaching the single cell. These data show that commonly accepted anatomical representations are oversimplified. We have incorporated the high-resolution anatomical data into mathematical simulations of cardiac electrical depolarisation. The data presented should have multidisciplinary impact. Since the rate of depolarisation is dictated by cardiac microstructure, and the precise orientation of the cardiomyocytes, our data should improve the fidelity of mathematical models. By showing the precise 3-dimensional relationships between the cardiac conduction system and surrounding structures, we provide new insights relevant to valvar replacement surgery and ablation therapies. We also offer a practical method for investigation of remodelling in disease, and thus, virtual pathology and archiving. Such data presented as 3D images or 3D printed models, will inform discussions between medical teams and their patients, and aid the education of medical and surgical trainees.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Stephenson, Robert S.","Atkinson, Andrew","Kottas, Petros","Perde, Filip","Jafarzadeh, Fatemeh","Bateman, Mike","Iaizzo, Paul A.","Zhao, Jichao","Zhang, Henggui","Anderson, Robert H.","Jarvis, Jonathan C.","Dobrzynski, Halina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-273616"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Jarvis, Jonathan C."],"country":["New Zealand","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Liverpool John Moores University","Newcastle University","University of Auckland","University of Manchester","University of Minnesota"],"keyword":["AXIS","Aortic Valve","Architecture","Atrioventricular Node","Computed tomography","Heart","Pacemaker","Reconstruction","sinoatrial node"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high resolution 000000000003 dimensional imaging of the human cardiac conduction system from microanatomy to mathematical modeling","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85026863488","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-273616","identifier":[{"id":"85026863488","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000406889500017","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC5543124","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28775383","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-fceab942-cace-4b0e-b1b2-08e65b683d37"],"keyword":["AORTIC-VALVE","ARCHITECTURE","ATRIOVENTRICULAR NODE","AXIS","COMPUTED-TOMOGRAPHY","HEART","HUMAN SINUS NODE","PACEMAKER","RECONSTRUCTION","SINOATRIAL NODE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4FA1BA2699CA394BF4FBE8955E439CD9"],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Comparative Medicine Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"liverpool john moores university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool John Moores University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of manchester","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Manchester","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of minnesota","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Minnesota","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"nz","key":"university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"gb","key":"newcastle university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Newcastle University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert S.","key":"stephensonpau","last":"Stephenson","locid":"858ae7d6-3a73-4db2-8eeb-bf4b6074b8f1","name":"Stephenson, Robert S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"atkinsonpau","last":"Atkinson","name":"Atkinson, Andrew","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Petros","key":"kottaspau","last":"Kottas","name":"Kottas, Petros","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Filip","key":"perdepau","last":"Perde","name":"Perde, Filip","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fatemeh","key":"jafarzadehpau","last":"Jafarzadeh","name":"Jafarzadeh, Fatemeh","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"batemanpau","last":"Bateman","name":"Bateman, Mike","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul A.","key":"iaizzopau","last":"Iaizzo","name":"Iaizzo, Paul A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichao","key":"zhaopau","last":"Zhao","name":"Zhao, Jichao","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Henggui","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Henggui","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert H.","key":"andersonpau","last":"Anderson","name":"Anderson, Robert H.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan C.","key":"jarvispau","last":"Jarvis","name":"Jarvis, Jonathan C.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Halina","key":"dobrzynskipau","last":"Dobrzynski","name":"Dobrzynski, Halina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28775383"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41598-017-07694-8","issn":["20452322"],"issue":"1","journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"7188","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026863488"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fceab942-cace-4b0e-b1b2-08e65b683d37"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"High resolution 3-Dimensional imaging of the human cardiac conduction system from microanatomy to mathematical modeling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-273616","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The 2014–2016 JET results are reviewed in the light of their significance for optimising the ITER research plan for the active and non-active operation. More than 60 h of plasma operation with ITER first wall materials successfully took place since its installation in 2011. New multi-machine scaling of the type I-ELM divertor energy flux density to ITER is supported by first principle modelling. ITER relevant disruption experiments and first principle modelling are reported with a set of three disruption mitigation valves mimicking the ITER setup. Insights of the L–H power threshold in Deuterium and Hydrogen are given, stressing the importance of the magnetic configurations and the recent measurements of fine-scale structures in the edge radial electric. Dimensionless scans of the core and pedestal confinement provide new information to elucidate the importance of the first wall material on the fusion performance. H-mode plasmas at ITER triangularity (H = 1 at βN ~ 1.8 and n/nGW ~ 0.6) have been sustained at 2 MA during 5 s. The ITER neutronics codes have been validated on high performance experiments. Prospects for the coming D–T campaign and 14 MeV neutron calibration strategy are reviewed.","author_count":1223,"contributors":["Litaudon, X.","Abduallev, S.","Abhangi, M.","Abreu, P.","Afzal, M.","Aggarwal, K.M.","Ahlgren, T.","Ahn, Jong Hyun","Aho-Mantila, L.","Aiba, N.","Airila, M.","Albanese, R.","Aldred, V.","Alegre, D.","Alessi, E.","Aleynikov, P.","Alfier, A.","Alkseev, A.","Allinson, M.","Alper, B.","Alves, E.","Ambrosino, G.","Ambrosino, R.","Amicucci, L.","Amosov, V.","Andersson Sundén, E.","Angelone, M.","Anghel, M.","Angioni, C.","Appel, L.","Appelbee, C.","Arena, P.","Ariola, M.","Arnichand, H.","Arshad, S.A.","Ash, A.","Ashikawa, N.","Aslanyan, V.","Asunta, O.","Auriemma, F.","Austin, Y.","Avotina, L.","Axton, M.D.","Ayres, C.","Bacharis, M.","Baciero, A.","Baião, D.","Bailey, Stephen","Baker, A.","Balboa, I.","Balden, M.","Balshaw, N.","Ba