person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yufeng","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Yufeng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Saeema","key":"ahmedkristensenpau","last":"Ahmed-Kristensen","locid":"1b7adf77-3491-42d2-b5c7-6e8ccf26a12f","name":"Ahmed-Kristensen, Saeema","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mike","key":"gregorypau","last":"Gregory","name":"Gregory, Mike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["14779056","17418178"],"issn_org":["14779056"],"issue":"3/4","journal":"International Journal of Product Development","pages":"171-173","publisher":"Inderscience Publishers","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Product Development","volume":"17"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4af9b176-6c2e-4c0f-891e-f3ba4fb6d95d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Editorial: Special Issue on International Engineering Operations: New Explorations of High Value Engineering and Service","type":"Editorial","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-326853","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"• It is well established that individual organisms can acclimate and adapt to temperature to optimize their functioning. However, thermal optimization of ecosystems, as an assemblage of organisms, has not been examined at broad spatial and temporal scales. • Here, we compiled data from 169 globally distributed sites of eddy covariance and quantified the temperature response functions of net ecosystem exchange (NEE), an ecosystem-level property, to determine whether NEE shows thermal optimality and to explore the underlying mechanisms. • We found that the temperature response of NEE followed a peak curve, with the optimum temperature (corresponding to the maximum magnitude of NEE) being positively correlated with annual mean temperature over years and across sites. Shifts of the optimum temperature of NEE were mostly a result of temperature acclimation of gross primary productivity (upward shift of optimum temperature) rather than changes in the temperature sensitivity of ecosystem respiration. • Ecosystem-level thermal optimality is a newly revealed ecosystem property, presumably reflecting associated evolutionary adaptation of organisms within ecosystems, and has the potential to significantly regulate ecosystem-climate change feedbacks. The thermal optimality of NEE has implications for understanding fundamental properties of ecosystems in changing environments and benchmarking global models.","author_count":72,"contributors":["Niu, Shuli","Luo, Yiqi","Fei, Shenfeng","Yuan, Wenping","Schimel, David","Law, Beverly E","Ammann, Christof","Arain, M Altaf","Arneth, Almut","Aubinet, Marc","Barr, Alan","Beringer, Jason","Bernhofer, Christian","Black, T Andrew","Buchmann, Nina","Cescatti, Alessandro","Chen, Jiquan","Davis, Kenneth J","Dellwik, Ebba","Desai, Ankur R","Etzold, Sophia","Francois, Louis","Gianelle, Damiano","Gielen, Bert","Goldstein, Allen","Groenendijk, Margriet","Gu, Lianhong","Hanan, Niall","Helfter, Carole","Hirano, Takashi","Hollinger, David Y","Jones, Mike B","Kiely, Gerard","Kolb, Thomas E","Kutsch, Werner L","Lafleur, Peter","Lawrence, David M","Li, Linghao","Lindroth, Anders","Litvak, Marcy","Loustau, Denis","Lund, Magnus","Marek, Michal","Martin, Timothy A","Matteucci, Giorgio","Migliavacca, Mirco","Montagnani, Leonardo","Moors, Eddy","Munger, J William","Noormets, Asko","Oechel, Walter","Olejnik, Janusz","Kyaw Tha Paw U, no-firstname","Pilegaard, Kim","Rambal, Serge","Raschi, Antonio","Scott, Russell L","Seufert, Günther","Spano, Donatella","Stoy, Paul","Sutton, Mark A","Varlagin, Andrej","Vesala, Timo","Weng, Ensheng","Wohlfahrt, Georg","Yang, Bai","Zhang, Zhongda","Zhou, Xuhui"],"cuid":["S02-097.61-018025"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","Canada","China","Czechia","Finland","France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Poland","Russia","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Agenzia Regionale per la Prevenzione e l'Ambiente dell'Emilia Romagna","Agroscope","All Global Affiliations","Alterra","Beijing Normal University","CNRS","Centre for Ecology and Hydrology","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Climate Research Division","Czech Academy of Sciences","Dresden University of Technology","Edmund Mach Foundation","European Commission Joint Research Centre Institute","Fudan University","Harvard University","Hokkaido University","INRAE","Johann Heinrich von Thunen Institute","Lund University","McMaster University","Monash University","Montana State University","National Center for Atmospheric Research","National Ecological Observatory Network","National Research Council of Italy","North Carolina State University","Northern Arizona University","Oak Ridge National Laboratory","Oregon State University","Pennsylvania State University","P